WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.682
For two days we handled alerts.

2
00:00:02.682 --> 00:00:10.487
But every alert comes from a security solution, and if that solution is missing, there is no alert at all.

3
00:00:10.487 --> 00:00:14.610
A quiet console can mean a safe network, or a blind one.

4
00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:21.604
Element 2 asks three questions: is it installed, is it operational, and can it clean the issue?

5
00:00:21.604 --> 00:00:25.359
This demonstration is question one, for the school.

6
00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.039
First, the rule.

7
00:00:28.039 --> 00:00:34.554
SOC-SOP-03 section A says which solutions each kind of host needs.

8
00:00:34.554 --> 00:00:41.858
Windows computers need all three: antivirus, EDR and the Wazuh SIEM agent.

9
00:00:41.858 --> 00:00:46.004
Linux servers need EDR and the SIEM agent.

10
00:00:46.004 --> 00:00:50.051
Isolated Tier 3 test PCs do not need EDR.

11
00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:58.427
Always start from the endpoint inventory, the list of computers the school owns, not from the console.

12
00:00:58.427 --> 00:01:06.343
Six endpoints: one Windows server, three workstations, a Linux portal server and a test PC in the computer lab.

13
00:01:07.444 --> 00:01:10.292
Now the console's coverage report.

14
00:01:10.292 --> 00:01:13.307
Count the rows: only five computers.

15
00:01:13.307 --> 00:01:15.988
MKT-PC-04 is missing completely.

16
00:01:15.988 --> 00:01:21.601
It was never enrolled, so the console does not even know it exists.

17
00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:29.308
That is a coverage gap, and the most dangerous kind, because nothing about it ever shows up.

18
00:01:30.408 --> 00:01:33.149
grep finds every Not installed.

19
00:01:33.149 --> 00:01:37.924
LIB-PC-02 is a Windows workstation without EDR: a gap.

20
00:01:37.924 --> 00:01:48.094
PORTAL-01 is a Linux server without the Wazuh agent: the SIEM receives nothing from the school portal, another gap.

21
00:01:48.094 --> 00:01:54.816
LAB-PC-15 has no EDR either, but it is a Tier 3 test PC, so that is allowed.

22
00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.205
Here is my coverage check.

23
00:01:58.205 --> 00:02:01.639
Three gaps to report to the Shift Lead.

24
00:02:01.639 --> 00:02:06.482
Notice that I report, I do not install anything myself.

25
00:02:06.482 --> 00:02:08.947
Fixing coverage is IT's job.

26
00:02:10.048 --> 00:02:10.926
Your turn.

27
00:02:10.926 --> 00:02:15.669
In the CTM Virtual Lab, choose Day 7 and Activity 7.1.

28
00:02:15.669 --> 00:02:19.534
Seventeen endpoints in the bank's inventory.

29
00:02:19.534 --> 00:02:24.453
Compare them with the console report and find every gap.

30
00:02:24.453 --> 00:02:27.615
Hint: count the lines of both files.

